From 4b96b5b987848a167eea35033284a95d22a006f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:02:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: Reject unmappable MPEG startup input

The preroll scanner reads vb2_plane_vaddr() before the stream writer
can reject a failed imported dma-buf CPU mapping. Return EFAULT before
scanning a NULL mapping, preserving the existing preparation error path
and all completion, reference and preroll token checks.

Change-Id: I17d26f75b24b05f865641f6d217cf99740ecb862
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
index 0ced55f37c86..1a80bff9d09c 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
@@ -840,6 +840,9 @@ static int mpeg12_multi_prepare_input(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 	bool slice = false, header = false;
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	if (!data)
+		return -EFAULT;
+
 	mutex_lock(&m->lock);
 	if (m->input_refs >= 2)
 		goto unlock;
-- 
2.47.3

